{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.H2GramArithmetic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.H2GramArithmetic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerFactorial","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Notation"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2GramMatrix_det_ne_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2GramMatrix_det_ne_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2GramArithmetic.lean#L84-L89","doc":"**`H_2` semisimple ⟺ nonzero Gram determinant ⟺ `[2]_q! ≠ 0`\n(sorry-free).**  Ties the concrete matrix determinant to Wenzl's\ncriterion at `n = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2GramMatrix_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2GramMatrix_det","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2GramArithmetic.lean#L77-L82","doc":"**The `H_2` Gram determinant equals `[2]_q²` (sorry-free).**  A direct\n`2×2` determinant: `det = 2(q²+1) - (q-1)² = (q+1)² = [2]_q²`.  This is\nthe actual regular-trace Gram determinant — the `n = 2` case of\n`det(Gram) = [n]_q!` (up to a unit) — now at the matrix level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2GramMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2GramMatrix","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2GramArithmetic.lean#L68-L74","doc":"**The `H_2(q)` regular-trace Gram matrix** in the basis `{1, σ}`.\nEntries are the observable traces `tr(L_{eᵢ eⱼ})`: `tr(1) = 2`,\n`tr(σ) = q-1` (companion-matrix trace of `σ² = (q-1)σ + q`),\n`tr(σ²) = tr((q-1)σ + q·1) = (q-1)² + 2q = q²+1`.  Taking the trace is\nthe observation step — the Gram *is* a matrix of observable results. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2_gram_det_ne_zero_iff_q_ne_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2_gram_det_ne_zero_iff_q_ne_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2GramArithmetic.lean#L57-L65","doc":"The criterion in bare-parameter form: `H_2(q)` is semisimple iff\n`q ≠ -1` (sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2_gram_det_ne_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2_gram_det_ne_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2GramArithmetic.lean#L50-L55","doc":"**`H_2` Gram-determinant criterion (sorry-free).**  The Gram\ndeterminant `det = (q+1)² = [2]_q²` is nonzero iff `[2]_q! ≠ 0` iff\n`q ≠ -1` — the `n = 2` instance of Wenzl's semisimplicity criterion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.h2_disc_eq_qInt_two_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.h2_disc_eq_qInt_two_sq","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2GramArithmetic.lean#L43-L48","doc":"**The `H_2` discriminant = `[2]_q²` (sorry-free).**  The discriminant\nof `X² - (q-1)X - q` is `(q-1)² + 4q = (q+1)²`, which is exactly the\nsquare of the quantum integer `[2]_q = 1 + q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.qFactorial_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.qFactorial_two","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2GramArithmetic.lean#L39-L41","doc":"`[2]_q! = 1 + q` (sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.qInt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.qInt_two","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/H2GramArithmetic.lean#L35-L37","doc":"`[2]_q = 1 + q` (sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0}]}